Wait, I made a mess in touchMove — I left unfinished logic and it doesn't actually apply look/move or pinch. Let me rewrite the touchMove function properly. The current edit has a broken touchMove with unused code. Let me fix it now.

Correct touchMove:
```js
function touchMove(e) {
  let lookDx = 0, lookDy = 0;
  for (const t of e.changedTouches) {
    const f = touchFingers.get(t.identifier);
    if (!f) continue;
    const dx = t.clientX - f.lx, dy = t.clientY - f.ly;
    f.lx = t.clientX; f.ly = t.clientY;
    f.moved += Math.abs(dx) + Math.abs(dy);
    if (touchGesture === 'look' && touchFingers.size === 1) { lookDx += dx; lookDy += dy; }
  }
  e.preventDefault();
  if (touchGesture === 'look' && touchFingers.size === 1) {
    cam.yaw += lookDx * 0.0025;
    const move = -lookDy / cam.zoom;
    const fwd = camForward();
    cam.x += fwd.x * move;
    cam.y += fwd.y * move;
    clampCam();
  }
  if (touchGesture === 'pinch' && touchFingers.size >= 2) {
    const ids = [...touchFingers.keys()];
    const a = touchFingers.get(ids[0]), b = touchFingers.get(ids[1]);
    const dist = Math.hypot(b.lx - a.lx, b.ly - a.ly);
    if (dist > 0 && pinch.startDist > 0) {
      const nextZoom = clamp(pinch.startZoom * dist / pinch.startDist, [0.35, 3.5]);
      cam.x = pinch.startCamX + pinch.startMx / pinch.startZoom - pinch.startMx / nextZoom;
      cam.y = pinch.startCamY + pinch.startMy / pinch.startZoom - pinch.startMy / nextZoom;
      cam.zoom = nextZoom;
      clampCam();
      pinch.startDist = dist;
      pinch.startZoom = nextZoom;
      pinch.startCamX = cam.x; pinch.startCamY = cam.y;
    }
  }
}
```

Wait — there's an issue with `clamp` signature: `clamp(v, range)` where range is an array [lo, hi]. In wheel code: `clamp(cam.zoom * (1 + dir), [0.35, 3.5])`. OK consistent.

Also `clamp` is defined as `function clamp(v, range) { return Math.max(range[0], Math.min(range[1], v)); }`. Good.

Also note in look mode, `lookDx`/`lookDy` accumulate across changedTouches — but in look mode only one finger so fine.

One subtlety: in touchMove for look mode, dx/dy computed against f.lx which was updated previous event — good per-frame deltas.

Now fix the broken touchMove.

